{
  "comment": "Menus and confirmation doors (docs/design/04 W-02, W-23; US-1.3; D-004). 'title' rows are in the owner order: Continue, Load, New, Journal, Custom Run, Settings, Quit (the co-op row exists with visible:false). Each row: id, labelKey (strings), action (continue | open | confirm), target screen and slots 'mode' for open, 'confirm' door id for confirm, 'enabledWhen' (always | hasValidSlot | targetBuilt) and 'visible'. Continue is shown disabled when no slot holds a valid save (shipped, AW:245). 'confirms' are W2 doors: question title, target identity, exact consequence, footer keys. 'policy' names a ui/confirmationPolicies.json policy; a DESTRUCTIVE policy gives the red, never-green primary. 'hold' makes the primary hold-to-confirm (holdMs is the holdConfirm token). 'single' shows one full-width action (the AI notice). 'occupiedBodyKey' replaces the body when the slot already holds a climb.",
